cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "avsec — secure video over an existing analog composite video path"
message: "If you use this testbed or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: RE22GDV
repository-code: "https://github.com/RE22GDV/avsec"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
keywords:
  - UAV video
  - analog composite video
  - CVBS
  - authenticated encryption
  - AEAD
  - Reed-Solomon
  - interleaving
  - multiple description coding
abstract: >-
  A research testbed that reproduces the LFSR block-permutation scheme for UAV
  analog video links proposed at ISITIA 2021, demonstrates experimentally that
  it provides no confidentiality, and builds a replacement on standard
  cryptography: digital source coding with per-segment AEAD and Reed-Solomon,
  carried as luminance levels through the same analog composite path. Includes a
  full experimental programme on both procedural material and real drone
  imagery, with every published number generated from a single recorded run.
